# One %s with padding width 100000000 — 100 MB > 64 MB cap.
# mew format width parser caps width at 100000, so we emulate by repeating
# smaller calls. But the cap should be on bi_format output: use a fmt like
# "%100000s" repeated N times via join, with N args "x" produced in parallel.
# Alternative simplest: single format call with fmt "%s" and arg = pre-built
# very long string via repeat. len goal > 64 MB.
big = repeat("A", 70000000)
print(len(format("%s", big)))
